   "widgets_values": [
    "HaDeS MOSS Suite - HMS v1 Converter (the eleventh video tutorial)\n\n1. Load any BF16 / FP16 MOSS-Image model in MOSS Loader (or connect a merge from Block Merger).\n2. Connect clip (mandatory: HMS v1 calibrates C1 + GPTQ on 7 fixed prompts through your model)\n   and optionally info -> recipe.\n3. Match hms_steps / hms_cfg / hms_sampler to your model:\n   - Base / SFT: 25 steps, CFG 2.5, er_sde / simple\n   - Turbo models: 8 steps, CFG 1.0, euler / simple\n   - Bulle d'Encre: 15 steps, CFG 2.5, euler / simple\n4. Output: ~3.96 GB safetensors in ComfyUI/output/diffusion_models, loadable with stock Load Diffusion Model.\n   On RTX 5090: conversion takes 8-10 min (~25 GB VRAM peak); inference uses ~11.6 GB VRAM and is ~2x faster.\n   Note: HMS v1 is a practical alternative to save VRAM; it never replaces full BF16 if you have the memory."
   ],
